From: programista-zacny <5969291+programista-zacny@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media_codecs: add the HEVC decoder, hide the secure AVC decoder

Two changes to the codec list, in one patch because both touch
media_codecs.xml (prepare-tree.sh checks each patch on its own).

Add OMX.Exynos.hevc.dec, the source-built component for the HEVC decoder
IP of the Exynos 5433 (the openmax patch installs it to /vendor/lib/omx/).
Limits are those of the HEVC IP: up to 1920x1088, 1080p60 in macroblocks
per second. No .secure entry: the kernel's HEVC driver registers no secure
node. Tested on the SM-T815 on 2026-11-08 with this entry on the device:
apps list OMX.Exynos.hevc.dec before c2.android.hevc.decoder and decode
through it. Logs: logs/omx-test3-hevc-20261108/.

Hide OMX.Exynos.avc.dec.secure (commented out, not removed). It configures
and opens the secure MFC node, but Widevine L1 decryption into it fails:
Samsung's liboemcrypto rejects the secure buffer ("wv_dash: Invalid secure
handle", then "WVCdm: Decrypt error", ERROR_DRM_UNKNOWN). The component
supports neither allocateNativeHandle nor metadata mode, so ACodec falls
back to the legacy secure buffer, which this liboemcrypto does not accept.
Apps that see a secure decoder open an L1 session first: Prime Video
failed and fell back (once to a black screen until replayed), HBO Max
failed and fell back to L3 with the non-secure hardware decoder. Without
the entry they go to L3 directly.
---
diff --git a/configs/media/media_codecs.xml b/configs/media/media_codecs.xml
index 6151b4d..a2e8b9b 100644
--- a/configs/media/media_codecs.xml
+++ b/configs/media/media_codecs.xml
@@ -123,6 +123,7 @@ Only the three quirks included above are recognized at this point:
             <Limit name="concurrent-instances" max="16"/>
             <Feature name="adaptive-playback" />
         </MediaCodec>
+        <!-- Hidden (gts210ltexx, 2026-11-08): Widevine L1 decrypt into this decoder fails ("Invalid secure handle" in liboemcrypto); apps that see it try L1 first and fail.
         <MediaCodec name="OMX.Exynos.avc.dec.secure" type="video/avc" >
             <Quirk name="requires-allocate-on-input-ports" />
             <Quirk name="requires-allocate-on-output-ports" />
@@ -136,6 +137,19 @@ Only the three quirks included above are recognized at this point:
             <Limit name="concurrent-instances" max="2"/>
             <Feature name="adaptive-playback" />
             <Feature name="secure-playback" required="true" />
+        </MediaCodec> -->
+        <MediaCodec name="OMX.Exynos.hevc.dec" type="video/hevc" >
+            <Quirk name="requires-allocate-on-input-ports" />
+            <Quirk name="requires-allocate-on-output-ports" />
+            <Quirk name="decoder-ignores-streamcorrupt-error" />
+            <Quirk name="video-controller-check-enable" />
+            <Limit name="size" min="64x64" max="1920x1088" />
+            <Limit name="alignment" value="2x2" />
+            <Limit name="block-size" value="16x16" />
+            <Limit name="blocks-per-second" min="1" max="489600" />
+            <Limit name="bitrate" range="1-50000000" />
+            <Limit name="concurrent-instances" max="4"/>
+            <Feature name="adaptive-playback" />
         </MediaCodec>
         <MediaCodec name="OMX.Exynos.vp8.dec" type="video/x-vnd.on2.vp8" >
             <Quirk name="requires-allocate-on-input-ports" />
diff --git a/configs/media/media_codecs_performance.xml b/configs/media/media_codecs_performance.xml
index 55bca84..26aa395 100644
--- a/configs/media/media_codecs_performance.xml
+++ b/configs/media/media_codecs_performance.xml
@@ -100,12 +100,13 @@
             <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-1280x720" range="25-45" />
             <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-1920x1080" range="10-20" />
         </MediaCodec>        
+        <!-- Hidden with the codec entry in media_codecs.xml.
         <MediaCodec name="OMX.Exynos.avc.dec.secure" type="video/avc" update="true" >
             <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-320x240" range="170-300" />
             <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-720x480" range="130-250" />
             <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-1280x720" range="130-250" />
             <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-1920x1080" range="100-180" />
-        </MediaCodec>
+        </MediaCodec> -->
         <MediaCodec name="OMX.Exynos.vp8.dec" type="video/x-vnd.on2.vp8" update="true" >
             <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-320x240" range="620-648" />
             <Limit name="measured-frame-rate-720x480" range="720-720" />
